## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Auvis project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using pnpm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `pnpm-lock.yaml` with resolved dependencies

**2. Analytics Integration - Main App**
- Modified `app/app/layout.tsx`:
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the body element
  - Follows Next.js App Router pattern as specified in the official documentation

**3. Analytics Integration - Demo App**
- Modified `demo/app/layout.tsx`:
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the body element
  - Ensures analytics tracking across both the main app and demo sections

### Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide for Next.js with the App Router:
- Used the `@vercel/analytics/next` package for Next.js-specific integration
- Placed the Analytics component at the root layout level to track all pages
- The component is placed at the end of the body tag, following React best practices
- No configuration file needed - analytics work out of the box once deployed to Vercel

### Verification

✅ Package successfully installed via pnpm
✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ TypeScript compilation passed
✅ No new linting errors introduced by the changes
✅ Analytics components properly integrated in both layout files
✅ Lock file (pnpm-lock.yaml) updated correctly

### Next Steps

To enable analytics:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel project dashboard
3. Analytics data will start appearing after users visit the deployed site

The Analytics component will automatically collect page views and web vitals metrics once the application is deployed to Vercel with Web Analytics enabled in the dashboard.
